  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its `description` says when to use the skill in terms of the user's task. It applies during design sessions and before changing code, tests or requirement text, even when the user only asks for a feature, bug fix, CLI flag, test, dependency bump or wording tweak. It also names `habeas-refactor` and `habeas-evidence` as alternatives where an agent could confuse them, which the requirement allows. No obligation is unmet, and no violation queries apply.",
